st 5 iterations discarded as fill/warmup; last 2 iterations before ramp-down (drain) excluded; fill/drain phases are reported separately (as their own overhead figure) but never folded into the steady-state bubble rate, since fill/drain inflates all schemes equally in kind but unequally in magnitude and would confound the near-zero claim. If the fork's timeline tool marks fill/drain boundaries, use them; otherwise detect steady state as iterations with stable T_iter (drift < 1% over a 10-iteration window) and cut the window conservatively inside it.\n\nInstruments (dual, as agreed):\n  (a) Megatron per-rank timers (forward/backward/comm/optimization elapsed times per rank per iteration) \u2014 primary, low overhead;\n  (b) torch.profiler (or equivalent trace export) on all pipeline ranks for a 5\u201310 iteration window in a subset of runs \u2014 independent cross-check of idle windows; used in at least one run per core cell.\n  (c) The fork's clock-profile/timeline visualization (context-based: the zero-bubble repo ships a timeline dump) for direct schedule-vs-measured comparison.\n\nTimeline-vs-measured mismatch analysis (turns the number into a diagnosis):\n  A \"mismatch\" = an idle window present in the measured per-rank timeline but absent in the planner's predicted schedule (i.e., the rank should have had work). Mismatch rate reported as fraction of predicted-busy time lost. Localization protocol:\n    - window coincides with cross-rank communication wait \u2192 classify comm wait (verify via NCCL/torch.distributed timeline markers);\n    - window follows an upstream stage's slow chunk \u2192 classify load imbalance (correlate with per-stage chunk durations);\n    - window varies across repeats with no systematic schedule position \u2192 classify synchronization skew / jitter (report variance across repeats);\n  Each ZB-2p run receives a mismatch taxonomy so the final claim reads \"near-zero, and residual bubbles come from X,\" not just a percentage.\n\nRun hygiene: lock clocks if permitted, pin ranks, record NCCL version, GPU model, driver, and the emitted schedule; identical seeds/data across arms within a cell; inter-run cooldown to rule out thermal drift; per-iteration timers logged to disk for offline recomputation.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n6. ANALYSIS PLAN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n  A1: per cell, mean \u00b1 std of absolute bubble rate across \u22653 repeats; report 95% CI (t-based, small n acknowledged).\n  A2: ordering test P2 via pairwise comparisons (Wilcoxon signed-rank across matched cells, or bootstrap CI on scheme differences; n is small \u2014 nonparametric preferred over ANOVA).\n  A3: near-zero test P1: absolute bubble rate \u2264 2% (pre-registered threshold) per ZB-2p cell; report every cell, including failures.\n  A4: planner fidelity: per ZB-2p cell, predicted vs measured timeline divergence (mismatch rate + taxonomy from \u00a75).\n  A5: stress analysis: ZB-2p bubble rate delta between balanced vs S1/S2 cells; determines whether near-zero survives real-world stressors.\n  A6: C3 sanity gate reported first; all downstream numbers conditional on it passing.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n7. SUCCESS / FAILURE CRITERIA\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n  CONFIRMED: ZB-2p shows absolute steady-state bubble rate \u2264 2% in all balanced core cells (single- and multi-node), with 95% CI upper bound < 5%, ordering P2 holds, and residual idle is taxonomized as comm/imbalance/skew with mismatch rate \u2264 ~5% of predicted-busy time.\n  PARTIALLY CONFIRMED: near-zero holds in single-node balanced cells but degrades measurably under imbalance or multi-node comm \u2014 then the answer is conditional and the taxonomy identifies which stressor breaks it.\n  NOT CONFIRMED: ZB-2p bubble rate materially exceeds threshold in balanced cells, or planner-predicted schedule and measured timeline diverge beyond mismatch tolerance, or C3 sanity gate fails (methodology invalid; redesign measurement before concluding anything about ZB-2p).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n8. FEASIBILITY ASSESSMENT\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n  Hardware: minimum 8 GPUs of one type for single-node cells; 2 nodes \u00d7 4\u20138 GPUs for multi-node cells. GPU-disabled here \u2014 execution assumed to happen on an external stand (stated assumption).\n  Memory: ZB-2p's higher activation footprint is an explicit resource constraint: budget a model configuration sized for the ZB-2p worst case; if OOM forces optimizer sharding, apply it identically across all three arms in that configuration and log it.\n  Runtime: ~44\u201360 runs \u00d7 (55\u201385 iterations) \u2248 a few hours of GPU wall time per configuration class; well within a one-day allocation per node-pair. Feasible.\n  Software: Megatron-LM fork with zero-bubble support; NCCL; torch.profiler. Network disabled in this sandbox \u2014 repo acquisition must occur on the execution stand.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n9. ASSUMPTIONS (vs. fixed requirements)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nFixed by task: design-only; ZB-2p activated via zero-bubble config flag (brief); no execution claimed.\nAssumed (not confirmed by local code): external multi-GPU stand availability; specific Megatron fork version matching the zero-bubble paper's code; availability of timeline dump utility; GPU clock control permissions; that compute dominates comm for the chosen model in single-node cells (needed for clean baseline sanity check).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n10. UNCERTAINTIES (open, resolved only by execution)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n  U1: Flag semantics --zero-bubble-max-pending-backward = 2\u00d7PP are brief-confirmed, not code-confirmed; runtime schedule-type verification (\u00a73) is the safeguard.\n  U2: ZB-2p memory pressure may constrain model size or require optimizer sharding; its effect on the comparison must be neutralized across arms.\n  U3: Whether a built-in bubble-rate metric exists in the fork is unknown; the dual-instrument methodology does not depend on it.\n  U4: Magnitude of residual bubbles under imbalance/inter-node comm \u2014 the central empirical question; taxonomy in \u00a75 is designed to answer \"why\" even if the answer is \"no.\"\n  U5: Small repeat count (n=3) limits statistical power; conclusions rest on effect size plus planner-fidelity analysis, not solely on significance tests.", "evidence": "Repository observations: /workspace contains only task.json (632 bytes) with the question text and documents.track.md stating \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\" A filesystem-wide search for megatron/zb/bubble repositories found nothing; torch/Megatron are not installed; environment declares gpu_enabled=false and network disabled. Therefore no code-level inspection of the planner was possible, and all fork-specific claims (flag semantics, timeline tool, schedule-type logging) are marked brief-confirmed or context-based rather than code-confirmed.\n\nDesign grounding: (1) bubble-rate metric and (p\u22121)/(m+p\u22121) prediction for 1F1B come from the Zero Bubble Pipeline Parallelism paper (Qi et al.) and standard pipeline-parallelism literature; (2) the three-arm comparison and the 2\u00d7PP activation value come from the same context plus the brief's note; (3) researcher-approved elements incorporated as instructed: absolute + relative bubble-rate reporting (\u00a75), explicit fill/drain exclusion window (\u00a75), mismatch taxonomy for planner-vs-measured comparison (\u00a75, A4), 1F1B sanity gate against (p\u22121)/(m+p\u22121) (C3, A6), and explicit single-node/multi-node split (\u00a72 node split rationale). Feasibility sized against the ~18-run minimum with repeats and stress cells added (~44\u201360 runs, few hours wall time). No experiment was run and no outcome is claimed.", "stage": "result", "assumptions": ["External multi-GPU stand available for execution: \u22658 GPUs of one type (single-node) and 2\u00d74\u20138 GPU nodes (multi-node), functioning NCCL", "Execution stand has the Megatron-LM zero-bubble fork available; versions match the zero-bubble-pipeline-parallelism project context", "The fork provides a timeline/clock-profile dump of the planned schedule (context-based, not verified locally)", "Clock control and per-rank profiling permissions are available on the stand", "Chosen model size is large enough that compute dominates communication in single-node cells (required for the 1F1B sanity gate to be meaningful), yet fits in memory under ZB-2p's higher activation footprint"], "uncertainties": ["U1: Flag semantics of --zero-bubble-max-pending-backward (=2\u00d7PP \u2192 ZB-2p regime) are brief-confirmed only; mitigated by runtime schedule-type verification from the fork's planner output", "U2: ZB-2p memory pressure may force optimizer sharding or smaller microbatches; handled as an explicit constraint applied identically across arms, but it could change absolute bubble numbers", "U3: Existence/format of a built-in bubble-rate metric in the fork is unknown; design relies on dual external measurement instead", "U4: Actual residual-bubble magnitude under stage imbalance and inter-node communication is unknown \u2014 this is the empirical question the design answers", "U5: n=3 repeats per cell limits statistical power; conclusions lean on effect sizes and planner-fidelity analysis rather than significance alone"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-fae64208f6564ce880dc380c484434bf", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "end_researcher_turn: {"answer": "EXPERIMENT DESIGN \u2014 \"Does ZB-2p achieve a near-zero bubble rate in practice when profiled on multiple GPUs?\"\n(Design-only document. No experiment has been run; /workspace contains no code, and all source-specific claims below are marked as either brief-confirmed or literature/context-based.)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n1. OBJECTIVE AND HYPOTHESIS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nObjective: Empirically determine whether the ZB-2p schedule (automatic planner output of the zero-bubble pipeline-parallelism Megatron-LM fork), activated via --zero-bubble-max-pending-backward = 2 \u00d7 (number of pipeline stages), achieves a near-zero pipeline bubble rate on real multi-GPU hardware, and \u2014 if it deviates \u2014 localize the cause.\n\nHypothesis H1 (from the Zero Bubble Pipeline Parallelism paper): ZB-2p reduces theoretical bubble to ~0, while 1F1B retains (p\u22121)/(m+p\u22121) and ZB-1p retains roughly (p\u22121)/(m+p\u22121) minus ~75% of it. Operational predictions:\n  P1: measured ZB-2p steady-state bubble rate \u2264 1\u20132% absolute (per scheme's own idle share of iteration time);\n  P2: measured ZB-2p bubble rate < ZB-1p < 1F1B (ordering test);\n  P3: deviations of ZB-2p from its planner's predicted timeline are attributable to identifiable causes (comm wait, stage imbalance, synchronization skew), not to the scheduler itself failing.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n2. CONFIGURATION MATRIX\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nFactor matrix (all arms run at identical model size, microbatch count m, global batch, and total GPU count per configuration):\n\n  Scheme (3): 1F1B | ZB-1p | ZB-2p\n  Pipeline size PP (2): 4 | 8\n  Placement (2): single-node (\u22648 GPUs, NVLink) | multi-node (e.g., 2 nodes \u00d7 4\u20138 GPUs, Ethernet/IB inter-node)\n  Stress scenarios (2, run for ZB-2p only unless resources allow all arms):\n    S1 stage-load imbalance: one stage's compute inflated ~20% (e.g., wider MLP) to see if ZB-2p's slack absorbs or leaks bubbles;\n    S2 high inter-node latency: place PP=8 across 2 nodes so T_comm/T_iter is elevated.\n\nCore matrix: 3 schemes \u00d7 2 PP sizes \u00d7 2 placements = 12 cells.\nStress extensions: 2 scenarios \u00d7 ZB-2p \u00d7 {PP=4, PP=8} \u00d7 2 placements = up to 8 cells.\nRepeats: \u22653 per cell \u2192 12 \u00d7 3 = 36 core runs + 8\u201324 stress runs \u2248 44\u201360 runs total. Each run: 5 warmup iterations (excluded) + 50 measured steady-state iterations (single-node) or 30 (multi-node, slower).\n\nNode split rationale: PP=4 and single-node PP=8 are single-node cells; PP=8 multi-node and all S2 cells are the multi-node subset (~1/3 of core cells) \u2014 this isolates the inter-node stress axis without doubling the whole matrix.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n3. ACTIVATION OF ZB-2p (brief-confirmed flag semantics)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n--zero-bubble-max-pending-backward set to 2 \u00d7 PP (e.g., PP=4 \u2192 8; PP=8 \u2192 16). Per the paper/fork context, this pushes the schedule into the ZB-2p regime (two backward chunks in flight per stage); the fork's automatic planner then emits the schedule. Verification at runtime: assert from the fork's log/planner output that the emitted schedule is labeled ZB-2p (the fork prints the schedule type); do not infer mode from the flag value alone. Memory note (context-based): ZB-2p holds more activations; if OOM occurs, enable optimizer sharding / reduce microbatch and record this as a deviation in the run log rather than silently changing the model size between arms.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n4. CONTROLS AND BASELINES\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n  C1 (primary baseline): 1F1B \u2014 textbook bubble rate predicted analytically as (p\u22121)/(m+p\u22121) for each (m, p) pair.\n  C2 (attribution control): ZB-1p \u2014 separates \"zero-bubble machinery exists\" from \"2p scheduling specifically drives bubble to zero.\"\n  C3 (measurement-validity control / sanity check): the 1F1B baseline's measured steady-state bubble rate must match (p\u22121)/(m+p\u22121) within a pre-set tolerance (e.g., \u00b120% relative or \u00b12 percentage points absolute). If it does not, the profiling methodology itself is suspect and all results are quarantined until the cause (timer overhead, window placement, sync skew) is fixed. This check is run first, before any ZB arm.\n  C4 (planner cross-check): for every ZB-2p run, extract the planner's predicted timeline and compare with the measured timeline.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n5. MEASUREMENT METHODOLOGY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nMetric definition (primary): bubble_rate = \u03a3_r idle_r / (p \u00d7 T_iter), where idle_r is time rank r is neither computing a forward/backward chunk nor doing overlapping communication within its schedule slot, and T_iter is the steady-state iteration time. Reported per scheme and per configuration as BOTH absolute (idle share of iteration time, %) and relative to the 1F1B baseline of the same cell.\n\nMeasurement window: strictly steady-state. First 5 iterations discarded as fill/warmup; last 2 iterations before ramp-down (drain) excluded; fill/drain phases are reported separately (as their own overhead figure) but never folded into the steady-state bubble rate, since fill/drain inflates all schemes equally in kind but unequally in magnitude and would confound the near-zero claim. If the fork's timeline tool marks fill/drain boundaries, use them; otherwise detect steady state as iterations with stable T_iter (drift < 1% over a 10-iteration window) and cut the window conservatively inside it.\n\nInstruments (dual, as agreed):\n  (a) Megatron per-rank timers (forward/backward/comm/optimization elapsed times per rank per iteration) \u2014 primary, low overhead;\n  (b) torch.profiler (or equivalent trace export) on all pipeline ranks for a 5\u201310 iteration window in a subset of runs \u2014 independent cross-check of idle windows; used in at least one run per core cell.\n  (c) The fork's clock-profile/timeline visualization (context-based: the zero-bubble repo ships a timeline dump) for direct schedule-vs-measured comparison.\n\nTimeline-vs-measured mismatch analysis (turns the number into a diagnosis):\n  A \"mismatch\" = an idle window present in the measured per-rank timeline but absent in the planner's predicted schedule (i.e., the rank should have had work). Mismatch rate reported as fraction of predicted-busy time lost. Localization protocol:\n    - window coincides with cross-rank communication wait \u2192 classify comm wait (verify via NCCL/torch.distributed timeline markers);\n    - window follows an upstream stage's slow chunk \u2192 classify load imbalance (correlate with per-stage chunk durations);\n    - window varies across repeats with no systematic schedule position \u2192 classify synchronization skew / jitter (report variance across repeats);\n  Each ZB-2p run receives a mismatch taxonomy so the final claim reads \"near-zero, and residual bubbles come from X,\" not just a percentage.\n\nRun hygiene: lock clocks if permitted, pin ranks, record NCCL version, GPU model, driver, and the emitted schedule; identical seeds/data across arms within a cell; inter-run cooldown to rule out thermal drift; per-iteration timers logged to disk for offline recomputation.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n6. ANALYSIS PLAN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n  A1: per cell, mean \u00b1 std of absolute bubble rate across \u22653 repeats; report 95% CI (t-based, small n acknowledged).\n  A2: ordering test P2 via pairwise comparisons (Wilcoxon signed-rank across matched cells, or bootstrap CI on scheme differences; n is small \u2014 nonparametric preferred over ANOVA).\n  A3: near-zero test P1: absolute bubble rate \u2264 2% (pre-registered threshold) per ZB-2p cell; report every cell, including failures.\n  A4: planner fidelity: per ZB-2p cell, predicted vs measured timeline divergence (mismatch rate + taxonomy from \u00a75).\n  A5: stress analysis: ZB-2p bubble rate delta between balanced vs S1/S2 cells; determines whether near-zero survives real-world stressors.\n  A6: C3 sanity gate reported first; all downstream numbers conditional on it passing.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n7. SUCCESS / FAILURE CRITERIA\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n  CONFIRMED: ZB-2p shows absolute steady-state bubble rate \u2264 2% in all balanced core cells (single- and multi-node), with 95% CI upper bound < 5%, ordering P2 holds, and residual idle is taxonomized as comm/imbalance/skew with mismatch rate \u2264 ~5% of predicted-busy time.\n  PARTIALLY CONFIRMED: near-zero holds in single-node balanced cells but degrades measurably under imbalance or multi-node comm \u2014 then the answer is conditional and the taxonomy identifies which stressor breaks it.\n  NOT CONFIRMED: ZB-2p bubble rate materially exceeds threshold in balanced cells, or planner-predicted schedule and measured timeline diverge beyond mismatch tolerance, or C3 sanity gate fails (methodology invalid; redesign measurement before concluding anything about ZB-2p).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n8. FEASIBILITY ASSESSMENT\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n  Hardware: minimum 8 GPUs of one type for single-node cells; 2 nodes \u00d7 4\u20138 GPUs for multi-node cells. GPU-disabled here \u2014 execution assumed to happen on an external stand (stated assumption).\n  Memory: ZB-2p's higher activation footprint is an explicit resource constraint: budget a model configuration sized for the ZB-2p worst case; if OOM forces optimizer sharding, apply it identically across all three arms in that configuration and log it.\n  Runtime: ~44\u201360 runs \u00d7 (55\u201385 iterations) \u2248 a few hours of GPU wall time per configuration class; well within a one-day allocation per node-pair. Feasible.\n  Software: Megatron-LM fork with zero-bubble support; NCCL; torch.profiler. Network disabled in this sandbox \u2014 repo acquisition must occur on the execution stand.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n9. ASSUMPTIONS (vs. fixed requirements)\n\u2