n effect size plus planner-fidelity analysis, not solely on significance tests.", "evidence": "Repository observations: /workspace contains only task.json (632 bytes) with the question text and documents.track.md stating \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\" A filesystem-wide search for megatron/zb/bubble repositories found nothing; torch/Megatron are not installed; environment declares gpu_enabled=false and network disabled. Therefore no code-level inspection of the planner was possible, and all fork-specific claims (flag semantics, timeline tool, schedule-type logging) are marked brief-confirmed or context-based rather than code-confirmed.\n\nDesign grounding: (1) bubble-rate metric and (p\u22121)/(m+p\u22121) prediction for 1F1B come from the Zero Bubble Pipeline Parallelism paper (Qi et al.) and standard pipeline-parallelism literature; (2) the three-arm comparison and the 2\u00d7PP activation value come from the same context plus the brief's note; (3) researcher-approved elements incorporated as instructed: absolute + relative bubble-rate reporting (\u00a75), explicit fill/drain exclusion window (\u00a75), mismatch taxonomy for planner-vs-measured comparison (\u00a75, A4), 1F1B sanity gate against (p\u22121)/(m+p\u22121) (C3, A6), and explicit single-node/multi-node split (\u00a72 node split rationale). Feasibility sized against the ~18-run minimum with repeats and stress cells added (~44\u201360 runs, few hours wall time). No experiment was run and no outcome is claimed.", "stage": "result", "assumptions": ["External multi-GPU stand available for execution: \u22658 GPUs of one type (single-node) and 2\u00d74\u20138 GPU nodes (multi-node), functioning NCCL", "Execution stand has the Megatron-LM zero-bubble fork available; versions match the zero-bubble-pipeline-parallelism project context", "The fork provides a timeline/clock-profile dump of the planned schedule (context-based, not verified locally)", "Clock control and per-rank profi